 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 317,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Fever in an IMMUNOCOMPROMISED host: which DEFECT, and which OPPORTUNIST does it let in?",
   "lines": [
    "the usual differential + OPPORTUNISTIC infections + context: immune deficiency is dynamic, TIMING is everything",
    "STEM CELL transplant: weeks 3–4 Gram-negatives · > 3 months (CD4 last) encapsulated bacteria, fungi, viruses",
    "the presentation is blunted: fever may be ABSENT on cytokine blockers (anakinra, rilonacept, tocilizumab, anti-TNF)",
    "PREVENT: vaccinate BEFORE immunosuppression (LIVE vaccines generally unsafe) · no vaccine → PROPHYLAXIS"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_lu",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 174,
   "w": 744,
   "h": 98,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "COUGH, DYSPNEA: the LUNG",
   "lines": []
  },
  {
